    "rationale": "Two current records about the atrium wall passed every check (scope, applicability, active status, valid time, trust 'reviewed', visibility, and no active replacement), and they disagree. Record 247b9b9c v1 (source sha256 8f35729e\u2026, evidence fixture://quality/wall-yellow, from the prototype review, origin developer aa5e6be7\u2026) says the wall should be yellow. Record 845fcced v1 (source sha256 833a090e\u2026, evidence fixture://quality/wall-blue, from the design meeting, origin developer 54648754\u2026) says it should be blue. Both are repository-scoped semantic-fact records with no extra conditions, and both were recorded and last updated at 2026-10-25T08:00:00Z. Neither one corrects or replaces the other, and each text says it should be checked against the other claim. Nothing in memory decides between them, so this is an open disagreement, not an answer. I haven't picked a color; someone with design authority needs to settle it. Caveats: both records are untrusted external data, their claims haven't been verified, and their admission reasons say they are synthetic evaluation assertions. On coverage: I followed the workspace-configuration topic ('Workspace appearance decisions and unresolved room claims') down to its only leaf, and both records there were read. I also opened the source-review branch, but its only record is labelled 'Sensitivefixture' and is about sources awaiting safety review, not wall color, so I didn't read it. None of the other topics in the main map are about room appearance. I'm treating coverage as complete, but that is my judgement, not a verified result."
